From 25603b3f38d5e8d3ed015aae1304d7be156fe931 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timur Ravilov <93673987+t0b1kent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 04:57:26 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT: ExecutableRangeInfo::NoTrap; validation modes 2/3
 and the range cache honour it; alias_* counters and JIT_REPORT_EVERY

FEXCore half of MACRUNNER_FEX_ALIAS_VIEWS (the tracker half is the next patch). A writable-code range can be one that page
protection cannot watch: an executable view of a section whose bytes change through ANOTHER view of the same pages (the RX half of
a W^X double mapping). ExecutableRangeInfo gets NoTrap (default false, every existing initializer is unchanged). When it is set:
- validation modes 2/3 do not skip the instruction as "whole host pages under the write trap" (Core.cpp), the trap does not see the write;
- the decoder remembers it next to Writable and MACRUNNER_FEX_RANGE_CACHE does not use the cached answer for such a range (Frontend.*).
Nothing sets NoTrap in this patch, so the emitted code is unchanged.

Diagnostics only: alias_found / alias_marked / alias_answered in the macrunner-fex-jit line, and MACRUNNER_FEX_JIT_REPORT_EVERY=<n>
(period of that line, default 4096) because the alias probes compile only a few dozen blocks and never reach 4096; the line buffer
grows to 1536 bytes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
